---
title: "Calculated Columns - Restrictions & Validation"
description: "Control what users can change in $framework Data Grid calculated columns: read-only columns, hidden menu items, restricted column references and custom validation of the Calculated Column dialog."
enterprise: true
---

These options control what users can do to [Calculated Columns](./calculated-columns/) through the grid's menus and the Calculated Column dialog.

## Read-Only Calculated Columns

Set `calculatedColumnReadOnly: true` to prevent users from changing a column's title, type or expression in the dialog. Users can choose **View Calculated Column** to inspect its definition. **Remove Calculated Column** is disabled in the column and cell context menus.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    calculatedColumns: true,
    columnDefs: [
        { field: 'revenue' },
        { field: 'cost' },
        {
            colId: 'grossMargin',
            calculatedExpression: '([revenue] - [cost]) / [revenue]',
            cellDataType: 'number',
            calculatedColumnReadOnly: true,
        },
    ],
};
```

The example keeps Gross Margin read-only, while Profit and user-created calculated columns remain editable.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Read-Only Calculated Columns" name="calculated-columns-read-only" /%}

If a column becomes read-only while its edit dialog is open, the dialog closes and any pending edits are discarded. Changes already applied are kept.

{% note %}
This setting restricts UI changes only: updating `columnDefs` and restoring [Grid State](./grid-state/) can still change or remove the column. Dialog-created columns ignore `defaultColDef.calculatedColumnReadOnly`, but [processColDef](./calculated-columns-dialog/#processcoldef) can make them read-only.
{% /note %}

### Hiding Menu Items

The calculated column actions are built-in menu items. To stop users adding, editing or removing calculated columns from the menus, filter them out of the default items with [getColumnMenuItems](./column-menu/#customising-the-menu-items) and [getContextMenuItems](./context-menu/#configuring-the-context-menu):

- `calculatedColumn`: **Add Calculated Column**, in the column menu.
- `editCalculatedColumn`: **Edit Calculated Column**, or **View Calculated Column** when the column is read-only, in the column menu.
- `removeCalculatedColumn`: **Remove Calculated Column**, in the column menu and the cell context menu.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    calculatedColumns: true,
    getColumnMenuItems: ({ defaultItems }) =>
        defaultItems.filter(
            item => item !== 'editCalculatedColumn' && item !== 'removeCalculatedColumn'
        ),
    getContextMenuItems: ({ defaultItems }) =>
        defaultItems?.filter(item => item !== 'removeCalculatedColumn'),
};
```

As with [read-only columns](#read-only-calculated-columns), this only removes the menu entries. Updating `columnDefs` and restoring Grid State can still change or remove the column.

## Restricting Column References {% #iscolumnreferenceable %}

Return `false` from `isColumnReferenceable` to exclude a column from the Columns picker, inline autocomplete and newly entered references. Use `calculatedColumn` to identify the column being edited, or `sourceColumn` for the column whose menu initiated **Add Calculated Column**. `sourceColumn` is only provided when adding a column; it is `null` when editing an existing column.

This example allows Salary references only when editing Bonus:

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    calculatedColumns: {
        isColumnReferenceable: ({ colDef, calculatedColumn }) => {
            if (colDef.field === 'salary') {
                return calculatedColumn?.getColId() === 'bonus';
            }
            return true;
        },
    },
};
```

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="IsColumnReferenceableParams" /%}

- The callback runs when the dialog opens.
- Existing permitted expressions can remain unchanged, and programmatic expressions are unrestricted unless explicitly revalidated with [`refreshCalculatedColumns()`](#refreshing-calculated-columns).
- Restricted edits disable Apply in deferred mode. In live mode, they are saved but display `#REF!` until corrected; reopening the dialog or restoring Grid State preserves the error.

This is a UI restriction, not a security boundary.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Dialog Reference Restrictions" name="calculated-columns-reference-restrictions" /%}

In the example, edit Bonus and Sales Target. Only Bonus can reference Salary.

## Validating Dialog Fields {% #getvalidationerrors %}

Use `getValidationErrors` to validate the dialog's title, type and expression. Return messages keyed by `headerName`, `cellDataType` or `calculatedExpression`, or `null` to accept the draft:

- Omitted fields and empty arrays are valid.
- Return or spread `internalErrors` to retain built-in feedback.
- The callback runs while typing, so keep it quick.
- Supply translated messages.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    calculatedColumns: {
        applyMode: 'deferred',
        getValidationErrors: ({ colDef, internalErrors }) => ({
            ...internalErrors,
            headerName: (colDef.headerName?.length ?? 0) > 30
                ? ['Use a title of at most 30 characters.']
                : internalErrors?.headerName,
        }),
    },
};
```

In the example, edit Sales Bonus and enter a title longer than 30 characters or an expression using `[Salary]` to see field-specific errors.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Custom Dialog Validation" name="calculated-columns-custom-validation" /%}

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="CalculatedColumnValidationParams" /%}

Editing the title or type revalidates the expression too, even when the expression is unchanged. Opening an editable live dialog rechecks expression rejections, even without edits.

{% note %}
This is a dialog guard, not a security boundary: `columnDefs` and Grid State restores do not run the callback. Rejections restored from Grid State remain blocked.
{% /note %}

### How Rejected Edits Behave

Any field error blocks Apply in deferred mode. In live mode, the outcome depends on the field:

| Rejected edit                                                         | Deferred mode  | Live mode                                                                                                                                                         |
| --------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Title or type rejected by `getValidationErrors`                       | Blocks Apply   | Keeps its last applied value, while other fields apply                                                                                                            |
| Expression rejected by `getValidationErrors`                          | Blocks Apply   | Saved, and displays `#ERROR!`, including when the callback returns built-in expression errors                                                                     |
| Expression referencing a column restricted by `isColumnReferenceable` | Disables Apply | Saved, and displays `#REF!` until corrected. Reference restrictions remain enforced, and use `#REF!` instead of `#ERROR!`, even when `getValidationErrors` is set |

## Refreshing Calculated Columns

Call `refreshCalculatedColumns()` after application validation rules change to revalidate expressions, update saved errors and recalculate cells and dependants without opening the dialog.

```js
api.refreshCalculatedColumns({ columns: ['profit'] });
// Omit columns to refresh all calculated columns.
api.refreshCalculatedColumns();
```

The refresh explicitly applies the current `getValidationErrors` and `isColumnReferenceable` rules:

- It includes read-only and programmatically defined columns.
- Applied expressions are checked with `sourceColumn: null`.
- Removed rules clear their saved rejections.
- Open dialogs also revalidate their drafts, without applying them or restarting the debounce.
- Validation changes emit `calculatedColumnChanged` with `source: 'api'`.

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-api/api.json" section="refresh" names=["refreshCalculatedColumns"] /%}
